/span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Ord/Basic.html#Ordering\">Ordering</a></span>}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">t</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Batteries/Recycling/RBTree/Basic.html#RBTree.RBSet\">RBSet</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">cmp</span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">cut</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Ord/Basic.html#Ordering\">Ordering</a></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Batteries/Recycling/RBTree/Basic.html#RBTree.RBSet\">RBSet</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">cmp</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`O(log n)`. Remove an element from the tree using a cut function.\nThe `cut` function is used to locate an element in the tree:\nit returns `.gt` if we go too high and `.lt` if we go too low;\nif it returns `.eq` we will remove the element.\n(The function `cmp k` for some key `k` is a valid cut function, but we can also use cuts that\nare not of this form as long as they are suitably monotonic.)\n","docLink":"./Batteries/Recycling/RBTree/Basic.html#RBTree.RBSet.erase","kind":"def","line":704,"name":"RBTree.RBSet.erase","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/3a067208130fab4154e6a4dd29efd07e3a9466bd/Batteries/Recycling/RBTree/Basic.lean#L704-L713"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Recycling/RBTree/Basic.html#RBTree.RBSet.insertMany\"><span class=\"name\">RBTree</span>.<span class=\"name\">RBSet</span>.<span class=\"name\">insertMany</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">ρ</span> : 